---
description: Load TypeSafe/Jev API key from env or gitignored .env; never commit or print it.
alwaysApply: true
---

When using the TypeSafe skill, Jev, or `typesafe-sdk`, authenticate with `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`.

- Read it from the process environment. If unset, load the gitignored `.env` at the repo root (`set -a && [ -f .env ] && . ./.env && set +a`).
- Do not print, log, or commit the value. Do not put it in PRs, skill files, notes, or docs.
- `.env.example` is the tracked empty template (`TYPESAFE_API_KEY=`).
- `TypeSafeClient()` reads `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` automatically once it is in the environment.
